  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">JeCCDO Citizens Engagement Program - Phase II</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">JeCCDO Citizens Engagement Program - Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outcome 1: Targeted women have improved their income and increasingly claim their rights and contribute to peace
Output 1.1: Women organized/strengthened in SHGs and engaged in profitable individual IGAs
Output 1.2: CLAs or WPF are engaged in advocacy, SA and peace building
Outcome 2: Government partners and Iddir-led CBOs have increased capacity and a common platform for jointly improving basic services and building peace
Output 2.1. Key government partners capacitated on SA and peace building tools
Output 2.2. Iddir-led CBOs are empowered to engage in IGA, SA, womens empowerment, and peacebuilding
Output 2.3. Gender-balanced SACs established/revitalized
Outcome 3: Citizens know their rights and ensure that local development initiatives respond to their priority needs. 
Output 3.1: Citizens are aware of service standards and service quality and priority needs are assessed
Output 3.2: Citizens and service providers agree on priority development needs and these are integrated into woreda plans and budgets
Output 3.3: Citizen priorities are implemented and jointly monitored</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Projektet syftar till att st&#xe4;rka lokalsamh&#xe4;llen s&#xe5; att de kan h&#xe5;lla lokala myndigheter ansvariga f&#xf6;r att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra tj&#xe4;nster, fr&#xe4;mja fred och j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet i Etiopien.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project are Empowering Communities to hold local governments accountable for improving services, fostering peace, and promoting gender equality in Ethiopia.</narrative>
  </description>
